# fixedbugs, defect 413, lane b13-land-addr, 2026-10-07: an `@` argument whose
# element is past the array's end. Panel 196's R1 reaches the element when the
# call is made, after every argument was computed, so the argument after it
# runs first, and its line is printed, and the call then aborts naming the
# index, before the callee runs. Until R1 the element was read where the
# argument was written, and the program aborted before `said` ran.
function set(@n: i64, k: i64)
    n @ k

function said(k: i64) -> i64
    print("said ", k)
    return k

function main()
    xs: [i64] @ [0]
    set(n: @xs[3], k: said(k: 5))
    print(xs[0])
